    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205336": {
      "title": "Student Worker, Programming Assistant",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Student Worker, Programming Assistant - Work Study & Campus Employment McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Student Worker, Programming Assistant - Work Study & Campus Employment Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Worker, Programming Assistant - Work Study & Campus Employment Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Engagement Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Oct 5, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 205336 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: Programming Assistant Effective Date: 03/02/2026 Reports to: Operations & Program Assistant Department: Office of Student Engagement Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: Roj Student Center, McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: 08/05/2026 to 05/25/2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Provide programming and support for office programs and rec lounge coverage. Responsibilities: Cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher Have and maintain a good disciplinary record at McDaniel College (i.e. not on disciplinary probation as of the start of or during the course of employment) Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team Commitment to creating and supporting an inclusive campus community Must be able to work a minimum of 4 hours per week Requirements: Qualifications: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College. Provide excellent customer service to anyone who visits the Office of Student Engagement. Maintain a positive atmosphere for anyone who visits the Office of Student Engagement. Communicate with supervisor and colleagues on a regular/consistent basis Good punctuality and attendance Keep spaces neat and organized Keep up with on campus events and activities Attend any training sessions provided by OSE Timely responses to staff e-mails Join GroupMe messaging service to ensure time response to coverage request. Other duties as assigned Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
